<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb vehicle exports up 5.0% yr/yr - industry.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb vehicle exports up 5.0% yr/yr - industry.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's vehicle exports rose 5.0 percent from a year earlier to 341,169 units in February, the Japan Automobile Manufacturers Association said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It was the ninth straight month of gains on a year-on-year basis.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of February exports with percentage changes from a year earlier:</p>
<p>			    FEB	   YR/YR CHANGE</p>
<p> Cars		  265,328	     +4.2</p>
<p> Trucks		 71,877	     +7.9</p>
<p> Buses		   3,964	     +2.9</p>
<p>Exports by destination:</p>
<p> Asia		   49,411	    -11.3</p>
<p> Mideast		25,626	    +13.2</p>
<p> Europe		 93,013	     -1.6</p>
<p> - EU		   79,111	     -2.2</p>
<p> North America     108,029	    +11.5</p>
<p> - U.S.		 98,434	     +9.6</p>
<p> Latin America	30,820	    +40.3</p>
<p> Africa		 12,690	    +20.2</p>
<p> Oceania		21,093	     -5.4</p>
<p> Other		     487	     -8.5</p>
<p>Exports by major manufacturers:</p>
<p> Toyota	  89,282	    -17.5</p>
<p> Nissan	  53,579	    +18.1</p>
<p> Mazda	   47,689	     +3.0</p>
<p> Mitsubishi    46,770	     +5.9</p>
<p> Honda	   43,650	    +37.2</p>
</text>
